# ─── Per-box pilot configuration (edit these when replicating to a new box) ───

# Where your source videos live. cameras.json source.uri values are RELATIVE to
# this dir (e.g. "20/20E.mp4"), so the same config works on any box.
VIDEO_DIR=/home/admin1/Videos/traffic_pilot_videos

# The Voyager SDK venv that has axelera-runtime + openvino installed (the host
# worker uses it). Override per box.
VOYAGER_VENV=/home/admin1/voyager-sdk/venv

# Compiled models mounted into the (future) worker container. Committed in-repo
# under ./models, so this rarely changes.
MODELS_DIR=/home/admin1/traffic-pilot/models

# Optional Redis auth (leave empty for the pilot).
REDIS_PASSWORD=
CONSUMERS=4

# Vehicle detector (2026-06-03): domain-calibrated stock yolov8s@640 master.
# Best on-AIPU accuracy/throughput of the candidates tested: +29% vehicles vs
# yolo26s (and +47% over the original yolo26n), no transformer-attention quant
# loss, 643 fps headroom. See tmp/DETECTION_ACCURACY_FINDINGS.md + the
# [[vehicle-model-yolo26s-upgrade]] memory.
# Rollback chain: comment these two lines -> yolo26n default cascade. Prior
# yolo26s build is at models/cascade-build-s (vehicle-plate-cascade-s.yaml).
CASCADE_YAML=/home/admin1/traffic-pilot/config/cascade/vehicle-plate-cascade-v8s.yaml
CASCADE_BUILD_ROOT=/home/admin1/traffic-pilot/models/cascade-build-v8s

# Cameras: app mode uses config/cameras.json (configured from the UI); `./start.sh
# test` overrides to config/cameras-test.json (4 RTSP demo streams from rtsp_sim).
# Leave CAMERAS_FILE unset so the UI owns cameras.json; set it only to pin a file.
# CAMERAS_FILE=
